-- title:
--   Orbit averages over a finite group agree modulo the commutator subgroup $[N,N]$
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a group, $N\trianglelefteq G$ a normal subgroup, and $[N,N]$ its commutator subgroup, generated by the commutators $ghg^{-1}h^{-1}$ with $g,h\in N$. Let a finite group $H$ act on a set $X$, and fix an enumeration $g_1,\dots,g_m$ of the elements of $H$ ($m=|H|$). For a map $w:X\to G$ the *orbit average* of $w$ at $x\in X$ is the ordered product
--   $$\mathrm{Av}_w(x)=w(g_1\cdot x)\,w(g_2\cdot x)\cdots w(g_m\cdot x)\in G .$$
--
--   **Theorem.** Let $x,y\in X$ lie in the same $H$-orbit, i.e. $y=h\cdot x$ for some $h\in H$, and suppose $w(g\cdot x)\in N$ for every $g\in H$. Then
--
--   $$
--   \mathrm{Av}_w(x)\,\mathrm{Av}_w(y)^{-1}\in[N,N].
--   $$
--
--   The two averages are products of the same factors in different orders, and the statement says that the reordering costs only an element of $[N,N]$. Iterating averaging therefore pushes differences along an orbit into deeper and deeper terms $N\supseteq[N,N]\supseteq\cdots$ of the derived series.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The enumeration is `groupList H`, the list `Finset.univ.toList` of the finite type $H$ (a fixed but unspecified order), the average is `orbitAverage w x`, and the commutator subgroup is `⁅N, N⁆`.
